{"key":"i10-s0337","rationale":"Idea:\n### 1. Architectural Innovation: Simplified SpikingMLP\n\n**What was implemented?**\nI have modified the `SpikingMLP` class by removing the `F.gelu` activation function that was previously applied between the two `SpikingLinear` layers. The `forward` method now directly passes the output of the first `SpikingLinear` layer (after dropout) to the second `SpikingLinear` layer:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nx, spike1 = self.fc1(x)\nx = F.gelu(x) # Removed line\nx, spike2 = self.fc2(self.dropout(x))\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nx, spike1 = self.fc1(x)\nx, spike2 = self.fc2(self.dropout(x))\n```\n\n**Why was it implemented?**\nThis modification significantly enhances the ","callouts":{"1":"Spike-rate loss: the block adds 0.01 · r̄ to the training loss, where r̄ is the mean firing rate over the block's spike trains, so training pushes the network toward sparser firing."},"notes":[{"text":"+ 0.01·r̄ loss","kind":"loss","novel":1},{"text":"no GELU in MLP","kind":"evolved"}],"meta":"Iteration 10 · sample 337  ·  GSA state update  ·  unstable run","nodes":{"n1":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L265-L266","tip":null},"g":{"label":"g proj","code":"L184","tip":null},"q":{"label":"q proj","code":"L180","tip":null},"k":{"label":"k proj","code":"L181","tip":null},"v":{"label":"v proj","code":"L182","tip":null},"f":{"label":"f proj","code":"L183","tip":null},"cq":{"label":"ShortConv","code":"L189","tip":null},"ck":{"label":"ShortConv","code":"L190","tip":null},"cv":{"label":"ShortConv","code":"L191","tip":null},"cf":{"label":"ShortConv","code":"L192","tip":null},"core":{"label":"GSA","code":"L50-L147","tip":null},"gn":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L215","tip":null},"silu":{"label":"SiLU","code":"L217-L218","tip":null},"gm":{"label":"×","code":"L217-L218","tip":null},"o":{"label":"o proj","code":"L221","tip":null},"a1":{"label":"+","code":"L277","tip":null},"n2":{"label":"RMSNorm","code":"L280-L281","tip":null},"fc1":{"label":"fc1","code":"L236","tip":null